WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.111 --> 00:00:03.221
- Cher once told me "If it
doesn't matter in five years,

00:00:03.221 --> 00:00:04.680
"it doesn't matter."

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:05.545
And I was like

00:00:05.545 --> 00:00:06.656
- Thank you Cher.

00:00:06.656 --> 00:00:07.847
- Truer words.

00:00:09.107 --> 00:00:10.821
- God, I wish Cher had told me something.

00:00:18.972 --> 00:00:19.909
Swapping.

00:00:19.909 --> 00:00:21.109
No, that's a terrible answer.

00:00:21.109 --> 00:00:21.887
- Well.

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:23.238
- Is it?

00:00:23.238 --> 00:00:25.784
- It might not be the key,
but it definitely helps.

00:00:25.784 --> 00:00:27.591
I think learning how to fight.

00:00:29.091 --> 00:00:29.992
For real!

00:00:29.992 --> 00:00:31.260
Not like spar.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.121
Because I think humans disagree a lot.

00:00:34.121 --> 00:00:35.109
It's going to happen.

00:00:35.109 --> 00:00:37.401
You can't, there's no
way to get around it.

00:00:37.401 --> 00:00:39.860
But if you learn how to
have healthy arguments,

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.837
I think it's the best
thing for a marriage.

00:00:41.837 --> 00:00:43.549
- My trick is I married someone

00:00:43.549 --> 00:00:47.057
eight billion times nicer
and kinder and more patient

00:00:47.057 --> 00:00:50.123
and then some reason he puts up with me

00:00:50.123 --> 00:00:51.756
and it's worked out well.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:59.826
- In truth, I became much more
comfortable as I grew older

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:04.737
and as you let go your desire

00:01:04.737 --> 00:01:07.883
to compare yourself to
everything and everyone.

00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:10.390
- You realize how unreasonable that is.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:14.077
- We are given, once you
can really understand

00:01:14.077 --> 00:01:17.317
we are given an unrealistic
and unobtainable idea

00:01:17.317 --> 00:01:19.524
and representation of beauty,

00:01:19.524 --> 00:01:21.230
you go "oh wait a minute!

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.574
"The whole thing's just
a joke and a trick?

00:01:23.574 --> 00:01:24.880
"Oh then who cares?"

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:28.043
- The worrying about what
other people think of you

00:01:28.043 --> 00:01:30.539
I think becomes so, so unimportant.

00:01:30.539 --> 00:01:34.355
- Also when you fill your
life with wonderful things

00:01:34.355 --> 00:01:36.404
and friends and love, you don't have time.

00:01:36.404 --> 00:01:39.327
You just don't have time
to worry about nonsense.

00:01:44.107 --> 00:01:46.009
Find what makes you unique.

00:01:46.009 --> 00:01:50.015
Because if you can be unique

00:01:50.015 --> 00:01:54.312
and be yourself,you are irreplaceable.

00:01:54.312 --> 00:01:56.359
But the minute you start to fall in line,

00:01:56.359 --> 00:01:57.800
you're a dime a dozen.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.622
- I remember when I was
never getting hired,

00:02:00.622 --> 00:02:04.429
which was good 20 or 22 years,

00:02:04.429 --> 00:02:07.256
and I thought maybe
I'll go into production

00:02:07.256 --> 00:02:08.660
and I'll stop the acting side of it

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.337
and I'll do this and I remember my mom

00:02:10.337 --> 00:02:11.650
which I thought she was
going to be thrilled

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.656
with that much more stable

00:02:13.656 --> 00:02:14.761
and she said "When are you going to

00:02:14.761 --> 00:02:16.186
"get back to doing what you do?"

00:02:16.186 --> 00:02:17.918
Doesn't matter if you're hired.

00:02:17.918 --> 00:02:19.480
Doesn't matter what the outcome is.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.953
You need to do what it is you do.

00:02:21.953 --> 00:02:23.594
So just kind of stay the course.

00:02:28.454 --> 00:02:30.729
- Is it really lame if I say my husband?

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:37.208
I mean, let's start first of
all, I have Stockholm syndrome.

00:02:37.208 --> 00:02:38.476
Let's start there.

00:02:38.476 --> 00:02:41.297
Okay, he captured me
about eight years ago.

00:02:41.297 --> 00:02:42.608
- It's true guys.

00:02:42.608 --> 00:02:44.587
- He has done a great
job of brainwashing me

00:02:44.587 --> 00:02:46.230
and I'm telling you, I am in.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:47.405
Okay?

00:02:47.405 --> 00:02:48.807
No, I'm a big fan of my husband.

00:02:48.807 --> 00:02:52.832
He's funny, he's kind,
he's committed to me

00:02:52.832 --> 00:02:56.357
and our daughters and a
thousand other wonderful things.

00:02:56.357 --> 00:02:57.913
And he just makes me smile.

00:02:57.913 --> 00:02:59.972
- Now I have to say
Ben too, but I mean it.

00:02:59.972 --> 00:03:03.916
He's my face, my best
friend, and he makes me laugh

00:03:05.356 --> 00:03:08.131
like gut laugh starting to pass out,

00:03:08.131 --> 00:03:10.590
I'm seeing sparkles
about four times a day.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.238
And I don't know, I don't know

00:03:12.238 --> 00:03:13.549
anything that's better than that.

00:03:13.549 --> 00:03:15.186
I knew Dax before you.

00:03:15.186 --> 00:03:15.968
- That's true.

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:17.038
- I could have been Mrs. Dax.

00:03:17.038 --> 00:03:17.904
We don't know.

00:03:17.904 --> 00:03:18.896
It was never offered.

00:03:18.896 --> 00:03:20.333
- I don't even want to
know if you guys hooked up.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.046
- Never!

00:03:21.046 --> 00:03:21.603
- Because I don't like,

00:03:21.603 --> 00:03:22.877
I don't even want to ask those questions.

00:03:22.877 --> 00:03:25.666
I wouldn't put it past either
of you, and that's fine.

00:03:25.666 --> 00:03:26.885
You were young, you were kids,

00:03:26.885 --> 00:03:28.081
and you were both gorgeous, it's fine.

00:03:28.081 --> 00:03:29.390
- Wouldn't it be weird if right now

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:32.169
I'm like "by the way,
we dated for six months.

00:03:32.169 --> 00:03:34.008
"On the DL."

